translated_text:
Article 19

1. Prevention of Violence Against Women as referred to in Article 18 letter a may be carried out in the following forms as follows:a. developing communication media, information, education and public campaigns;
b. developing educational materials and curricula;
c. developing safe transportation systems and public spaces;
d. establishing early detection systems, security and integrated complaint services in industrial areas, companies, residential areas, educational environments, Islamic boarding schools and other public spaces;
e. providing consultation, information, education, and counseling services;
f. developing policies related to safe and friendly schools/madrasahs, boarding schools, Islamic boarding schools, and universities;
g. establishing and developing cadres, communities, and groups from among youth, students, santri (Islamic boarding school students), university students, journalists, social media influencers, educators, and religious leaders;
h. conducting education and advocacy to owners, managers and/or social media users;
i. developing protection systems and special support for vulnerable women groups;
j. conducting awareness-raising for perpetrators;
10-
k. increasing the capacity of regional governments, government agencies, institutions, community institutions, business sector, Islamic boarding schools, community organizations, media, religious leaders, community leaders and communities;
l. conducting cooperation with religious institutions, community social institutions, service institutions, universities, Islamic boarding schools, media, youth organizations, religious leaders and community leaders; andm. conducting socialization of laws and regulations.
2. Forms of prevention of Violence Against Women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

text:
Pasal 20

Perempuan korban kekerasan mendapatkan hak sebagai  berikut:
a. hak untuk dihormati harkat dan martabat sebagai  manusia;
b. hak pemulihan;
c. hak menentukan sendiri keputusannya;
d. hak mendapatkan kemudahan akses informasi;
e. hak atas kerahasiaan;
f. hak atas rehabilitasi sosial;
g. hak atas penanganan pengaduan secara cepat, tepat,  nyaman dan sesuai kebutuhan;
h. hak korban dan keluarganya untuk mendapatkan  kemudahan dalam proses peradilan;
i. hak atas pendampingan; danj. hak rasa aman.

translated_text:
Article 20

Women victims of violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as human beings;
b. the right to recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain easy access to information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling that is fast, appropriate, comfortable and according to needs;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance; andj. the right to security.

text:
Pasal 21

Pelayanan terhadap perempuan korban kekerasan dapat  dilakukan melalui:
a. penerimaan laporan dan/atau penjangkauan korban  kekerasan;
b. pemberian informasi tentang hak korban kekerasan;
c. fasilitasi pemberian layanan kesehatan;
d. fasilitasi pemberian layanan penguatan psikologis; e. fasilitasi pemberian layanan psikososial, rehabilitasi  sosial, pemberdayaan sosial, pemulangan, dan  reintegrasi sosial;
f. penyediaan layanan hukum;
g. identifikasi kebutuhan pemberdayaan ekonomi;
h. identifikasi kebutuhan penampungan sementara untuk  korban kekerasan dan keluarga korban kekerasan yang  perlu dipenuhi segera;
i. fasilitasi kebutuhan korban kekerasan penyandang  disabilitas;
11-
j. koordinasi dan kerja sama atas pemenuhan hak korban  kekerasan dengan lembaga lainnya; dank. pemantauan pemenuhan hak korban kekerasan oleh  aparatur penegak hukum selama proses acara  peradilan.

translated_text:
Article 21

Services for women victims of violence may be carried out through:
a. receiving reports and/or outreach to victims of violence;
b. providing information about the rights of victims of violence;
c. facilitating the provision of health services;
d. facilitating the provision of psychological strengthening services; e. facilitating the provision of psychosocial services, social rehabilitation, social empowerment, return, and social reintegration;
f. providing legal services;
g. identifying economic empowerment needs;
h. identifying temporary shelter needs for victims of violence and families of victims of violence that need to be fulfilled immediately;
